{"name":"Monkey Island","hex":"#553b39","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"monkey island","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of flying bridge."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monkey_island"}],"entries":[{"title":"Monkey Island","blocks":[{"text":"Monkey Island is a series of adventure games. The first four games were produced and published by LucasArts, earlier known as Lucasfilm Games. The fifth was developed by Telltale Games with LucasArts, while the sixth was developed by Terrible Toybox with Lucasfilm Games and Devolver Digital."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Monkey_Island_Logo.svg/330px-Monkey_Island_Logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monkey_Island","wikidata":"Q533239"},{"title":"Monkey Island (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Monkey Island is the seventh studio album by American rock band the J. Geils Band, though it is credited with the shortened band name of \"Geils\", the only album in their catalog for which this was done. The album was released on June 9, 1977, by Atlantic Records."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/72/J._Geils_Band_-_Monkey_Island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monkey_Island_(album)","wikidata":"Q3860900"},{"title":"Monkey","blocks":[{"text":"Monkey is a common name that may refer to most mammals of the infraorder Simiiformes, also known as simians. Traditionally, all animals in the group now known as simians are counted as monkeys except the apes. Thus monkeys, in that sense, constitute an incomplete paraphyletic grouping; alternatively, if apes (Hominoidea) are included, monkeys and simians are synonyms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Ubud_Monkey_Family.jpg/330px-Ubud_Monkey_Family.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monkey","wikidata":"Q1367"},{"title":"Island","blocks":[{"text":"An island or isle is a piece of land, distinct from a continent, completely surrounded by water. There are continental islands, which were formed by being split from a continent by plate tectonics, and oceanic islands, which have never been part of a continent. Oceanic islands can be formed from volcanic activity, grow into atolls from coral reefs, and form from sediment along shorelines, creating barrier islands. River islands can also form from sediment and debris in rivers. Artificial islands are those made by humans, including small rocky outcroppings built out of lagoons and large-scale land reclamation projects used for development."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg/330px-Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Island","wikidata":"Q23442"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2b/FOMI.png/330px-FOMI.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2b/FOMI.png/330px-FOMI.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"FOMI: The second game's opening scene","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFOMI.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/96/NOTH.png/330px-NOTH.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/96/NOTH.png/330px-NOTH.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"NOTH: The game's opening scene","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANOTH.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/ca/MITDT.jpg/330px-MITDT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/ca/MITDT.jpg/330px-MITDT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A screenshot from The Devil's Triangle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMITDT.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/44/TODI.png/250px-TODI.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/44/TODI.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/44/TODI.png/250px-TODI.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cover image of The Treasure of Drunk Island","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATODI.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/59/ManiacIsland.jpg/330px-ManiacIsland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/59/ManiacIsland.jpg/330px-ManiacIsland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The cover of The Mistery of Maniac Island","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AManiacIsland.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ef/NIAR.png/330px-NIAR.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/ef/NIAR.png/330px-NIAR.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A screenshot from Al Gurbish in... Nick it & Run!!!, an adventure game exhibition with many references to classic LucasArts and Sierra On-Line titles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANIAR.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/BrownSpiderMonkey_%28edit2%29.jpg/500px-BrownSpiderMonkey_%28edit2%29.jpg?utm_sou